Article 21
(1) Regional Government is obligated and responsible to implement efforts to prevent the occurrence of Violence against Women in the form of: a. collecting data and information about victims of violence and laws and regulations; b. conducting education about anti-Violence against Women values;
c. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of Protection for victims of violence;
d. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of Protection for victims of violence; and e. preparing reports on the implementation of Protection for women victims of violence.
(2) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of Violence against Women, Regional Government is obligated to provide and organize services for victims in the form of
a. establishing and facilitating the implementation of integrated service institutions for Victims by involving community elements; and
b. encouraging community awareness of the importance of Protection for Victims.
(3) Regional Government in carrying out obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians or other persons who are legally responsible for Victims.
(4) To prevent the occurrence of acts of Violence against Women, Regional Government undertakes efforts as follows:
a. conducting counseling and socialization regarding matters concerning Violence against Women;
b. conducting socialization of women's rights; c. seeking to improve education for women;
d. opening skills courses for women to support the economic needs of families;
e. creating employment opportunities for women; f. providing counseling to immediately report to local authorities if Violence against Women occurs;
g. empowering Social Community Organizations and women's organizations to increase women's knowledge and insight;
h. establishing Women's Protection Complaint Posts; and i. forming work networks in violence prevention efforts.

